1
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:19,099
And yes, you're right.

2
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,901
I'm pissed whenever I see you.
Do you know why?

3
00:00:21,901 --> 00:00:24,333
Because I remember what you did to me.

4
00:00:24,334 --> 00:00:26,200
And every time I remember what you did to me,

5
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,677
I want to kick you and crush you
to fine pieces.

6
00:00:29,677 --> 00:00:32,100
But it doesn't mean
that I don't want to see you anymore.

7
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,766
And that doesn't mean

8
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:36,450
that all my feelings for you
will just go away.

9
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:38,434
Even if you turn the world upside down,

10
00:00:38,434 --> 00:00:40,387
it's still you who my heart wants.

11
00:00:40,387 --> 00:00:42,356
- Don't you want it?
- Of course, I want to.

12
00:00:42,356 --> 00:00:43,491
I can't hear it.

13
00:00:43,491 --> 00:00:45,226
I like Florence.

14
00:00:45,226 --> 00:00:48,963
Hey, neighbors, Florence has a boyfriend!

15
00:00:51,699 --> 00:00:53,303
I like you.

16
00:00:54,235 --> 00:00:56,670
I like Florence!

17
00:00:57,538 --> 00:01:00,608
I'm going to a brunch,
so it's okay for me to skip breakfast.

18
00:01:00,608 --> 00:01:03,177
Brunch? We know you'll be with Florence.

19
00:01:03,177 --> 00:01:06,313
Just give her my kisses.

20
00:01:06,313 --> 00:01:08,981
Me too, give her my hugs and kisses.

21
00:01:10,985 --> 00:01:12,886
Me too, Nero.

22
00:01:14,197 --> 00:01:18,100
Of course, don't forget Mr. Dencio...

23
00:01:20,594 --> 00:01:22,429
But wait, Nero,
why did you pick me up this early?

24
00:01:22,429 --> 00:01:23,497
What's happening?

25
00:01:23,497 --> 00:01:26,066
Today is the first day to road happiness.

26
00:01:26,066 --> 00:01:31,097
And I'm planning to celebrate that
with the longest date in history.

27
00:01:31,097 --> 00:01:32,787
I'm so sorry to intrude,

28
00:01:32,787 --> 00:01:35,209
but can I talk to Florence
for a couple of minutes?

29
00:01:35,209 --> 00:01:39,847
In fairness, you have a fighting spirit.

30
00:01:39,847 --> 00:01:43,450
But it's still wrong
that you resorted to blackmail.

31
00:01:43,450 --> 00:01:45,176
Thank you, Florence.

32
00:01:45,176 --> 00:01:49,023
You know what, the way that I see it,

33
00:01:49,023 --> 00:01:52,393
it's Nero who won the jackpot
in your relationship.

34
00:01:52,393 --> 00:01:54,261
You're awesome, Florence.

35
00:01:54,261 --> 00:01:59,566
And truly,
I sincerely wish you and Nero happiness.

36
00:02:45,813 --> 00:02:47,242
Who is she?

37
00:02:48,262 --> 00:02:51,336
Her name is Florence Dela Cruz.

38
00:02:52,753 --> 00:02:55,623
Do you remember the computer guy
who did an approximation

39
00:02:55,623 --> 00:02:59,512
of your baby's appearance
if she happens to grow up?

40
00:03:00,995 --> 00:03:04,665
Of course, I didn't believe
that the Computer Graphics Specialist

41
00:03:04,665 --> 00:03:08,502
can approximate the appearance of Celestina

42
00:03:08,502 --> 00:03:11,171
if she grows up into a young woman,

43
00:03:11,171 --> 00:03:14,267
by uploading her baby picture.

44
00:03:16,307 --> 00:03:17,745
Look.

45
00:03:17,745 --> 00:03:20,299
That is the rendered picture.

46
00:03:22,683 --> 00:03:24,994
That's Celestina's baby picture.

47
00:03:28,188 --> 00:03:34,402
I have a strong feeling
that this is your missing daughter, Celestina.

48
00:03:34,402 --> 00:03:38,166
I believe that this girl is my granddaughter.

49
00:03:40,467 --> 00:03:43,904
I know you thought it was crazy,

50
00:03:43,904 --> 00:03:48,416
but I already saw her in Levante.

51
00:03:56,408 --> 00:03:58,928
I thought my eyes played tricks on me,

52
00:03:58,928 --> 00:04:03,791
but then I saw her again
in Garpidio's mansion.

53
00:04:03,791 --> 00:04:05,188
Grandpa Garp?

54
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:09,891
So you're Florence Dela Cruz?

55
00:04:15,069 --> 00:04:20,574
Since then, I have been curious and obsessed.

56
00:04:20,574 --> 00:04:23,031
She never disappeared from my sight.

57
00:04:24,093 --> 00:04:27,329
Grilled Chicken Buddies for life!

58
00:04:32,186 --> 00:04:34,588
Seriously, my daughter is still alive?

59
00:04:34,588 --> 00:04:37,725
My daughter with Alyanna is still alive.
Celestina is still alive?

60
00:04:37,725 --> 00:04:39,689
Yes.

61
00:04:41,595 --> 00:04:43,222
Dad, where is she?

62
00:04:43,222 --> 00:04:45,210
Where is she? I'll go to her. Where is she?

63
00:04:45,210 --> 00:04:47,000
Lorenzo, calm down.

64
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,703
- Just take it easy.
- How can I calm down?

65
00:04:49,703 --> 00:04:52,506
After all this time,
my daughter is still alive.

66
00:04:52,506 --> 00:04:54,108
Lorenzo, please.

67
00:04:54,108 --> 00:04:56,310
Just take it easy.

68
00:04:56,310 --> 00:05:00,180
Look, we need to be careful
in dealing with this

69
00:05:00,180 --> 00:05:03,762
or else we lose the opportunity
to get her back.

70
00:05:10,491 --> 00:05:12,431
So what's your plan?

71
00:05:14,194 --> 00:05:15,869
Okay, everyone,

72
00:05:15,869 --> 00:05:21,425
make sure
that our vegetables are cut correctly and nicely,

73
00:05:21,425 --> 00:05:23,251
especially you...

74
00:05:24,805 --> 00:05:28,575
Florence and her parents are our visitors.

75
00:05:28,575 --> 00:05:33,480
It's a shame
if the food we prepare is not delicious.

76
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,516
Serafica, relax.

77
00:05:35,516 --> 00:05:38,218
They will not judge us as a top chef.

78
00:05:38,218 --> 00:05:40,421
They know our capacity.

79
00:05:40,421 --> 00:05:43,390
Take it easy. Things are going fine.

80
00:05:43,390 --> 00:05:44,958
Oh my, Grandpa Garp.

81
00:05:44,958 --> 00:05:48,262
Federico is so judgmental.

82
00:05:48,262 --> 00:05:50,497
You said it.

83
00:05:50,497 --> 00:05:52,332
It's like he's from the Supreme Court.

84
00:05:52,332 --> 00:05:55,147
He's so judgmental.

85
00:05:55,147 --> 00:05:56,811
Really? Seriously?

86
00:05:56,811 --> 00:05:58,272
Don't appeal anymore.

87
00:05:58,272 --> 00:06:01,376
You can go to the Court of Appeals
to show off.

88
00:06:03,343 --> 00:06:04,645
Nero, what's that?

89
00:06:04,645 --> 00:06:06,662
It looks like you're staring too much
at what you're cooking.

90
00:06:06,662 --> 00:06:09,030
Tight guarding.

91
00:06:09,030 --> 00:06:10,725
This is a special Adobo, Grandpa Garp.

92
00:06:10,725 --> 00:06:13,959
It's Adobo without soy sauce,
just vinegar and salt.

93
00:06:13,959 --> 00:06:15,717
Is that possible?

94
00:06:15,717 --> 00:06:17,424
Why?

95
00:06:17,424 --> 00:06:19,059
If there's no soy sauce,

96
00:06:19,059 --> 00:06:21,686
you have to stare at it
thoroughly so it can be cooked?

97
00:06:21,686 --> 00:06:23,865
Do you have a laser beam in your eyes?

98
00:06:23,865 --> 00:06:25,701
"Do you have a laser beam in your eyes"?

99
00:06:25,701 --> 00:06:27,601
You're being a smart alec.

100
00:06:27,601 --> 00:06:29,569
That's dry Adobo.

101
00:06:29,569 --> 00:06:32,240
You need to keep an eye on the meat.

102
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:35,837
Look, it gets cooked in its own fats.

103
00:06:35,837 --> 00:06:39,773
It needs perfect timing.

104
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:41,908
What is this mess about?

105
00:06:41,908 --> 00:06:44,451
Oh, you're here.
Come on, boys. Give us a hand.

106
00:06:44,451 --> 00:06:45,833
Let's help finish this.

107
00:06:45,833 --> 00:06:49,403
We're going to make a nice feast
for the family of Florence.

108
00:06:49,403 --> 00:06:51,538
Come on! Help out.

109
00:06:51,538 --> 00:06:53,440
What can you contribute?

110
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:56,176
I'll be making a Paella Valenciana

111
00:06:56,176 --> 00:06:59,679
that is Paella Venduras and Paella Negra.

112
00:07:03,450 --> 00:07:05,851
As for me, I'll make sushi.

113
00:07:07,521 --> 00:07:10,554
- That's delicious.
- I'll take care of the mango pie.

114
00:07:14,328 --> 00:07:18,598
Wow, delicious.

115
00:07:19,265 --> 00:07:22,269
Florence, is it okay if we're bringing
cooked food there?

116
00:07:22,269 --> 00:07:24,238
Yes, of course, Mother. Grandpa Garp is kind.

117
00:07:24,238 --> 00:07:26,836
He'll appreciate this so much.

118
00:07:27,608 --> 00:07:30,444
You know, I don't want to be judgmental,

119
00:07:30,444 --> 00:07:32,780
but according to my judgment,

120
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:36,049
it seems there's no delicious food
cooked there.

121
00:07:36,049 --> 00:07:38,656
That's why, they are relying on their chefs.

122
00:07:41,355 --> 00:07:43,991
Florence, why are you dressed that way?

123
00:07:43,991 --> 00:07:47,394
Later, you might look grumpy there.

124
00:07:47,394 --> 00:07:51,131
Mother, it looks like we're going there
for an engagement.

125
00:07:51,131 --> 00:07:53,534
And besides, the people there know me,

126
00:07:53,534 --> 00:07:56,303
so even if I'm wearing a sack,
they will not judge me.

127
00:07:56,303 --> 00:07:57,805
What? What do you mean by wearing a sack?

128
00:07:57,805 --> 00:08:00,941
What's important is
you'll look presentable there.

129
00:08:00,941 --> 00:08:02,509
I look presentable.

130
00:08:02,509 --> 00:08:04,311
- No, you better prepare.
- I already look presentable!

131
00:08:04,311 --> 00:08:07,648
And you too, Federico!
How come you're not yet dressed?

132
00:08:07,648 --> 00:08:10,818
But how about my huge body?

133
00:08:10,818 --> 00:08:13,520
Go ahead and change.

134
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:15,122
Hey, who is that?

135
00:08:15,973 --> 00:08:17,591
Who is that?

136
00:08:17,591 --> 00:08:19,841
The car is beautiful.

137
00:08:27,901 --> 00:08:29,942
Grandpa Roger!

138
00:08:44,863 --> 00:08:47,763
Almost 17 years ago...

139
00:08:49,089 --> 00:08:52,731
A huge crime happened against my family.

140
00:08:57,598 --> 00:08:59,903
Alyanna!

141
00:09:03,070 --> 00:09:05,927
<i>And no one here can imagine the pain.</i>

142
00:09:06,807 --> 00:09:08,467
And what's painful is

143
00:09:08,467 --> 00:09:13,146
that they did not only take away
one life that day.

144
00:09:13,146 --> 00:09:14,548
My grandchild?

145
00:09:14,548 --> 00:09:16,717
My grandchild.

146
00:09:16,717 --> 00:09:17,751
Where is the baby?

147
00:09:17,751 --> 00:09:19,319
Have you seen a baby?

148
00:09:19,319 --> 00:09:22,856
We didn't notice a baby.

149
00:09:22,856 --> 00:09:24,984
Sir, did you notice anything there?

150
00:09:26,226 --> 00:09:28,328
Nothing, Don Rogelio.

151
00:09:37,871 --> 00:09:39,742
Lorenzo...

152
00:09:41,337 --> 00:09:43,500
They found Alyanna.

153
00:09:45,746 --> 00:09:47,531
She's gone.

154
00:09:48,415 --> 00:09:50,304
<i>How about Celestina?</i>

155
00:09:51,985 --> 00:09:54,390
They can't find her.

156
00:09:56,823 --> 00:09:59,793
<i>They never found her.</i>

157
00:09:59,793 --> 00:10:02,596
<i>No one saw the baby.</i>

158
00:10:02,596 --> 00:10:07,401
So, everyone assumed
that my granddaughter died.

159
00:10:07,401 --> 00:10:10,689
That Celestina was a victim too.

160
00:10:13,941 --> 00:10:19,095
But there's always a part of me
that believed my grandchild is still alive.

161
00:10:20,948 --> 00:10:22,349
Everybody thought I was crazy,

162
00:10:22,349 --> 00:10:27,220
even my own son thought
that I was being unreasonable.

163
00:10:27,220 --> 00:10:31,084
But no matter what everyone said,

164
00:10:31,084 --> 00:10:35,322
that's what I believe
because that's what my heart is telling me.

165
00:10:39,224 --> 00:10:41,395
And I was right.

166
00:10:44,404 --> 00:10:49,242
And I was right because the moment I saw you,

167
00:10:49,242 --> 00:10:52,412
my belief
that my granddaughter is still alive grew stronger.

168
00:10:52,412 --> 00:10:54,959
And that's you, Florence.

169
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:09,930
You are my missing granddaughter.

170
00:11:09,930 --> 00:11:12,712
You are Celestina Almero.

171
00:11:29,249 --> 00:11:32,953
This is a huge mistake, Don Rogelio.

172
00:11:32,953 --> 00:11:36,092
Florence is our daughter.

173
00:11:36,092 --> 00:11:38,645
We are her real parents.

174
00:11:41,094 --> 00:11:43,196
She's is really our daughter.

175
00:11:43,196 --> 00:11:47,300
Our sympathies to the death of Alyanna

176
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:49,156
and your grandchild.

177
00:11:51,405 --> 00:11:53,805
But this is a huge mistake.

178
00:11:54,841 --> 00:11:57,870
Are you serious, Federico?

179
00:11:57,870 --> 00:12:01,034
Can you stand by your lie?

180
00:12:03,650 --> 00:12:06,058
Grandpa Roger, please.

181
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:08,422
Why are you doing this to us now?

182
00:12:08,422 --> 00:12:10,773
Because that's the truth.

183
00:12:11,756 --> 00:12:18,429
I came here to give your parents
a chance to come clean.

184
00:12:21,034 --> 00:12:23,341
Don Rogelio.

185
00:12:25,705 --> 00:12:29,034
We didn't do anything wrong.

186
00:12:32,345 --> 00:12:38,498
Alright, then we have
to welcome an investigation.

187
00:12:43,790 --> 00:12:52,165
The truth is I asked my son, Lorenzo,
to become reasonable

188
00:12:52,165 --> 00:12:56,423
and don't do any drastic action.

189
00:12:56,423 --> 00:12:58,710
That's why, he's not here.

190
00:12:58,710 --> 00:13:01,640
And maybe that's for the better.

191
00:13:02,811 --> 00:13:09,845
Because if Lorenzo was here,
he would be unreasonable.

192
00:13:14,087 --> 00:13:17,970
That's why I'm here to give you a warning.

193
00:13:19,126 --> 00:13:24,644
We're going to exhaust every legal remedy

194
00:13:24,644 --> 00:13:28,972
to bring Florence back to her real family.

195
00:13:28,972 --> 00:13:33,181
So you can be returned to us, the Almeros.

196
00:13:39,012 --> 00:13:43,850
So, this is not the last time
you're going to see me.

197
00:13:43,850 --> 00:13:50,380
Please don't do anything
that will put you in danger.

198
00:14:07,607 --> 00:14:09,242
Did they arrive already?

199
00:14:09,242 --> 00:14:11,645
I just called the guardhouse.

200
00:14:11,645 --> 00:14:14,050
No one has arrived yet.

201
00:14:18,785 --> 00:14:22,588
Excuse me, Grandpa Garp,
I'll just call Florence.

202
00:14:36,703 --> 00:14:39,377
What are you doing?

203
00:14:40,307 --> 00:14:41,441
We're leaving.

204
00:14:41,441 --> 00:14:43,939
We'll go to a faraway place.

205
00:14:44,811 --> 00:14:47,681
Federico, have you gone mad?

206
00:14:47,681 --> 00:14:51,551
Didn't you hear what Don Rogelio said?

207
00:14:51,551 --> 00:14:55,922
Let's not do anything
that will put us in danger.

208
00:14:55,922 --> 00:14:59,426
Do you think we can escape from the Almeros?

209
00:14:59,426 --> 00:15:01,228
I don't care.

210
00:15:01,228 --> 00:15:03,830
They can't take my daughter from me.

211
00:15:03,830 --> 00:15:06,906
Federico, think!

212
00:15:07,934 --> 00:15:11,773
It's as if we're saying we committed a crime.

213
00:15:12,706 --> 00:15:18,345
Mother, Father, can you please
explain to me what's happening?

214
00:15:18,345 --> 00:15:21,648
Why is Grandpa Roger saying
that I'm his granddaughter?

215
00:15:21,648 --> 00:15:25,151
Why is he saying that I'm an Almero?

216
00:15:25,151 --> 00:15:29,370
Father, what's the truth?

217
00:15:40,767 --> 00:15:42,421
The truth is...

218
00:15:44,292 --> 00:15:46,624
your mother and I couldn't conceive a child.

219
00:15:51,483 --> 00:15:54,314
No matter what we did,

220
00:15:54,314 --> 00:16:00,663
we were never blessed with a baby
to complete our family.

221
00:16:15,568 --> 00:16:20,173
<i>I love your mother so much, but sometimes,</i>

222
00:16:20,173 --> 00:16:24,778
<i>I can't avoid thinking about
my biggest failure to her</i>

223
00:16:24,778 --> 00:16:28,080
<i>because I can't give her a child.</i>

224
00:16:45,732 --> 00:16:48,168
I'm sorry, Federico and Lydia.

225
00:16:48,168 --> 00:16:53,126
But with your situation right now,
you can't have a child.

226
00:17:20,066 --> 00:17:21,301
Is that you?

227
00:17:21,301 --> 00:17:24,004
Huh? That's not me.

228
00:17:24,004 --> 00:17:25,743
What was that?

229
00:17:27,411 --> 00:17:28,696
Oh no...

230
00:17:28,696 --> 00:17:31,148
Did you hear something?

231
00:17:31,148 --> 00:17:32,447
What?

232
00:17:35,148 --> 00:17:37,682
- Something is moving in the back.
- Huh?

233
00:17:37,682 --> 00:17:39,282
What's that?

234
00:17:41,827 --> 00:17:44,095
Hold on...

235
00:17:46,026 --> 00:17:48,761
Oh no, what's that?

236
00:19:08,889 --> 00:19:12,126
We just thought...

237
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:18,409
that you are the answer to our prayers.

238
00:19:20,854 --> 00:19:23,530
That you're heaven-sent.

239
00:19:27,607 --> 00:19:32,053
That you are the baby
we've been asking from God.

240
00:19:36,184 --> 00:19:38,606
We closed our eyes...

241
00:19:39,706 --> 00:19:46,012
and didn't bother to ask how a baby ended up

242
00:19:46,012 --> 00:19:49,547
in the back of the delivery truck
I was driving.

243
00:19:51,184 --> 00:19:59,159
And we promised
that we will love you completely.

244
00:19:59,159 --> 00:20:02,811
That we will love you like our own daughter.

245
00:20:07,433 --> 00:20:08,789
- Sorry...
- Florence?

246
00:20:08,789 --> 00:20:10,365
Florence!

247
00:20:14,717 --> 00:20:16,809
Nero?

248
00:20:16,809 --> 00:20:18,945
Florence?

249
00:20:18,945 --> 00:20:20,459
Nero.

250
00:20:48,975 --> 00:20:52,633
Why does it seem
like you always show up at the perfect time?

251
00:20:53,546 --> 00:20:57,850
Whenever I need you, you suddenly appear.

252
00:20:57,850 --> 00:21:00,820
I was calling you earlier.

253
00:21:00,820 --> 00:21:04,457
I wanted to ask why you haven't arrived.

254
00:21:04,457 --> 00:21:09,795
But when you didn't answer,
I decided to go to you.

255
00:21:10,964 --> 00:21:15,034
Did Grandpa Garp get mad
that we failed to make it?

256
00:21:15,034 --> 00:21:16,769
Don't think about that.

257
00:21:16,769 --> 00:21:19,205
I'll explain it to them.

258
00:21:22,942 --> 00:21:27,713
I'm sorry
your plans didn't push through again.

259
00:21:28,414 --> 00:21:32,899
I'm also sorry if I can't stop crying.

260
00:21:36,723 --> 00:21:39,042
There's no reason for you to be sorry.

261
00:21:40,059 --> 00:21:41,589
Just cry.

262
00:21:42,749 --> 00:21:45,409
I'm always here by your side.

263
00:21:47,667 --> 00:21:51,504
Nero, what should I do?

264
00:21:51,504 --> 00:21:53,973
The truth is I don't know what to do.

265
00:21:53,973 --> 00:21:57,143
I don't know what I should feel.

266
00:21:57,143 --> 00:21:59,155
How would I feel

267
00:21:59,155 --> 00:22:02,615
if everything I believed while growing up
suddenly collapsed,

268
00:22:02,615 --> 00:22:05,132
and everything is not true?

269
00:22:05,133 --> 00:22:09,666
Should I get mad at Mother and Father
because they lied to me?

270
00:22:09,667 --> 00:22:10,156
Florence...

271
00:22:10,156 --> 00:22:14,761
Or should I turn my back on them
and go to my real family?

272
00:22:14,761 --> 00:22:18,665
Or should I tell the Almeros
to stop bothering us

273
00:22:18,665 --> 00:22:21,901
and just let me be,

274
00:22:21,901 --> 00:22:25,471
because I'm not their missing granddaughter?

275
00:22:25,471 --> 00:22:30,176
I'm not an Almero.
I'm a Dela Cruz and that's the real me.

276
00:22:30,176 --> 00:22:34,513
That's the truth I believed, Nero.

277
00:22:37,183 --> 00:22:38,622
But...

278
00:22:40,920 --> 00:22:44,157
why is this happening to me?

279
00:22:44,157 --> 00:22:46,392
I've been doing okay.

280
00:22:46,392 --> 00:22:50,029
I'm happy with my life
with my father and mother.

281
00:22:50,029 --> 00:22:53,066
I don't need this kind of complication.

282
00:22:53,066 --> 00:22:55,268
Did I do something wrong?

283
00:22:55,268 --> 00:23:00,072
Did I do something bad
for all this to happen to me?

284
00:23:04,877 --> 00:23:09,397
Florence, it's not your fault.

285
00:23:09,397 --> 00:23:12,559
Bad things happen even to good people.

286
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:15,872
If only...

287
00:23:18,157 --> 00:23:21,327
If only I can give you my heart,

288
00:23:21,327 --> 00:23:24,657
so I'd be the one to feel
all the heaviness and pain

289
00:23:24,657 --> 00:23:27,413
you're feeling right now.

290
00:23:29,102 --> 00:23:30,718
Let it be me.

291
00:23:32,038 --> 00:23:33,960
Just let it be me.

292
00:24:15,782 --> 00:24:18,548
What happened? What was their reaction?

293
00:24:19,886 --> 00:24:21,830
Denial.

294
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:26,472
Looking desperate at their attempt
to stand by their lies.

295
00:24:26,472 --> 00:24:29,462
Why didn't you bring Celestina home?

296
00:24:29,462 --> 00:24:33,299
Firstly, her name is Florence.

297
00:24:33,299 --> 00:24:37,464
I don't think she'll respond
to the name Celestina.

298
00:24:37,464 --> 00:24:39,272
So whether we like it or not,

299
00:24:39,272 --> 00:24:41,574
we need to recognize the fact
that she grew up

300
00:24:41,574 --> 00:24:45,077
with a different identity,
with a different family.

301
00:24:45,077 --> 00:24:49,282
Secondly, she must come to us on her own.

302
00:24:49,282 --> 00:24:52,185
She should voluntarily come to us.

303
00:24:52,185 --> 00:24:58,724
Because if we force her,
the more she'll resist being an Almero.

304
00:24:58,724 --> 00:25:02,065
How can we be assured
that she'll come to us voluntarily?

305
00:25:02,065 --> 00:25:05,164
Look, for all I know, maybe her fake parents
are packing their things

306
00:25:05,164 --> 00:25:06,732
so they can take my daughter away.

307
00:25:06,732 --> 00:25:09,202
Baste is there.

308
00:25:09,202 --> 00:25:12,518
And I have people who are spying
and looking after the Dela Cruz family.

309
00:25:12,518 --> 00:25:16,642
That's why, even if they leave,
I can follow them wherever they go.

310
00:25:16,642 --> 00:25:19,946
But how can we be so sure
that Celestina will come here,

311
00:25:19,946 --> 00:25:22,915
I mean, Florence?

312
00:25:22,915 --> 00:25:26,152
Florence is a very smart girl.

313
00:25:26,152 --> 00:25:29,005
She knows what is at stake here.

314
00:25:29,005 --> 00:25:31,757
I think she can figure it out on her own.

315
00:25:31,757 --> 00:25:34,961
The moment she realizes the consequences

316
00:25:34,961 --> 00:25:38,798
of the things the parents she recognizes
are doing right now,

317
00:25:38,798 --> 00:25:42,435
she will make the right decision
for everybody.

318
00:25:42,435 --> 00:25:43,870
What if she won't do it?

319
00:25:43,870 --> 00:25:46,472
What if she won't come here?

320
00:25:46,472 --> 00:25:48,708
She has nowhere to hide.

321
00:25:48,708 --> 00:25:54,379
I will personally look for her
and drag her back here.

322
00:26:28,581 --> 00:26:30,419
Florence?

323
00:26:32,074 --> 00:26:33,583
My child.

324
00:26:36,153 --> 00:26:37,890
Have you eaten?

325
00:26:37,890 --> 00:26:40,014
I'll prepare food for you.

326
00:26:40,014 --> 00:26:41,739
No need, Mother.

327
00:26:41,739 --> 00:26:44,006
I'm okay.

328
00:26:44,006 --> 00:26:47,033
Where is Nero? Why didn't you let him in?

329
00:26:47,033 --> 00:26:49,790
I told him to go home

330
00:26:49,790 --> 00:26:54,657
and apologize to Grandpa Garp on our behalf
for failing to go for dinner.

331
00:26:56,430 --> 00:26:58,557
By the way, Florence.

332
00:26:58,557 --> 00:27:01,314
We spoke to Iking earlier.

333
00:27:01,314 --> 00:27:06,299
He knows a lawyer
who can help us with our situation.

334
00:27:06,299 --> 00:27:09,055
We'll talk to the lawyer right away

335
00:27:09,055 --> 00:27:14,742
so we'd find out what's the best thing to do
with our situation right now.

336
00:27:16,948 --> 00:27:20,677
Can we really do it, Mother?

337
00:27:20,677 --> 00:27:24,094
Can we afford to pay a lawyer?

338
00:27:25,321 --> 00:27:28,908
You heard what Don Rogelio said, right?

339
00:27:28,908 --> 00:27:33,118
They won't stop until they get you back.

340
00:27:36,482 --> 00:27:40,225
We won't easily give in, Florence.

341
00:27:42,028 --> 00:27:48,494
We're not related, but you're still my child.

342
00:27:48,494 --> 00:27:52,331
We're one family here.

343
00:27:52,331 --> 00:27:55,714
You're connected to our hearts.

344
00:27:56,417 --> 00:28:03,341
I won't allow them
to take you away from us just like that.

345
00:28:05,444 --> 00:28:09,348
Mother, just let it be.

346
00:28:09,348 --> 00:28:12,323
I'll talk to them first.

347
00:28:13,034 --> 00:28:17,323
I'll talk to Grandpa Roger.

348
00:28:17,323 --> 00:28:23,429
And if they really see me as an Almero,

349
00:28:23,429 --> 00:28:25,977
their granddaughter,

350
00:28:25,977 --> 00:28:29,160
maybe they will listen to me, right?

351
00:28:29,160 --> 00:28:30,269
But, Florence...

352
00:28:30,269 --> 00:28:31,760
Don't worry, Mother.

353
00:28:33,053 --> 00:28:36,291
I can do this.

354
00:28:37,502 --> 00:28:39,917
I'm cause of this problem,

355
00:28:39,917 --> 00:28:44,555
that's why I can find a way to solve this.

356
00:28:50,571 --> 00:28:52,961
Don't cry, Mother.

357
00:29:07,373 --> 00:29:10,469
We love you so much.

358
00:29:24,911 --> 00:29:28,403
I noticed the first time I saw Florence

359
00:29:28,403 --> 00:29:31,251
that she looks kind of familiar.

360
00:29:32,297 --> 00:29:38,642
She had this uncanny resemblance
to the late Alyanna Almero.

361
00:29:39,854 --> 00:29:43,989
So, you're Florence Dela Cruz.

362
00:29:50,861 --> 00:29:55,134
Sorry if I was surprised
because when I saw you,

363
00:29:55,134 --> 00:29:56,908
I remembered someone.

364
00:29:58,173 --> 00:30:06,233
Still, it's unbelievable
that the missing daughter of Lorenzo

365
00:30:06,233 --> 00:30:08,602
is Florence Dela Cruz.

366
00:30:10,622 --> 00:30:12,829
How is Florence?

367
00:30:13,993 --> 00:30:16,662
You know, Florence, Grandpa.

368
00:30:16,662 --> 00:30:19,563
She'll overcome everything
that is thrown at her.

369
00:30:20,733 --> 00:30:24,336
Yes, but this situation is very difficult.

370
00:30:24,336 --> 00:30:27,707
Her parents, Lydia and Federico,

371
00:30:27,707 --> 00:30:30,649
they're in a lot of trouble.

372
00:30:32,078 --> 00:30:34,847
Most likely they'll be accused
that they had something to do

373
00:30:34,847 --> 00:30:37,858
with the death of Alyanna Almero.

374
00:30:40,386 --> 00:30:42,982
That's what I'm afraid of, Grandpa.

375
00:30:43,943 --> 00:30:48,828
Tell Florence
that we're ready to help with whatever she needs.

376
00:30:48,828 --> 00:30:52,064
We won't think twice about it,
and will help her.

377
00:30:52,064 --> 00:30:55,768
She's family and we always protect our own.

378
00:30:55,768 --> 00:30:56,969
Thank you, Grandpa.

379
00:30:56,969 --> 00:30:59,006
I'll let her know that.

380
00:31:02,274 --> 00:31:05,945
According to our lawyer,
there will be a preliminary investigation.

381
00:31:05,945 --> 00:31:07,747
Was there a crime committed?

382
00:31:07,747 --> 00:31:10,516
What were the facts of the case?

383
00:31:10,516 --> 00:31:14,887
And how did Celestina end up...

384
00:31:14,887 --> 00:31:17,088
with the Dela Cruz Family.

385
00:31:20,526 --> 00:31:22,627
Sir, you have a visitor.

386
00:31:41,013 --> 00:31:42,481
Hello.

387
00:31:42,481 --> 00:31:44,503
Good day.

388
00:32:05,437 --> 00:32:07,940
I'm sorry... I'm sorry.

389
00:32:07,940 --> 00:32:10,009
You remind me so much of your mother.

390
00:32:10,009 --> 00:32:13,479
You know what?
She should be proud of you, Celestina...

391
00:32:13,479 --> 00:32:15,747
I'm sorry, I mean Florence.

392
00:32:17,316 --> 00:32:18,783
I'm sorry...

393
00:32:19,838 --> 00:32:23,167
I'm sorry if I'm being emotional...

394
00:32:23,167 --> 00:32:26,157
because I never thought I'd see you again.

395
00:32:29,040 --> 00:32:32,700
I told you, the moment you see Florence,

396
00:32:32,701 --> 00:32:36,768
there'll be no denying that she is an Almero.

397
00:32:37,469 --> 00:32:38,671
Have a seat.

398
00:32:38,671 --> 00:32:40,706
Have you met your grandfather?

399
00:32:40,706 --> 00:32:43,876
Have a seat. Have you eaten?
Do you want something to drink?

400
00:32:43,876 --> 00:32:44,877
Baste?

401
00:32:44,877 --> 00:32:45,811
- Yes, Sir?
- Get us something to drink.

402
00:32:45,811 --> 00:32:47,145
Yes, Sir.

403
00:32:54,720 --> 00:32:58,724
Actually, the reason why I'm here now...

404
00:32:58,724 --> 00:33:02,160
is that I want to talk to both of you.

405
00:33:05,130 --> 00:33:11,269
I want to talk to you
about my mother and father.

406
00:33:22,882 --> 00:33:24,450
So...

407
00:33:24,450 --> 00:33:26,320
did we do well last night?

408
00:33:27,219 --> 00:33:31,257
It was okay,
it managed to get in the top five.

409
00:33:31,257 --> 00:33:32,758
- Top five?
- Yup.

410
00:33:32,758 --> 00:33:36,495
Didn't I even reach the semis?

411
00:33:36,495 --> 00:33:39,431
Perhaps next time, you'll be the champion.

412
00:33:39,431 --> 00:33:43,034
Then I'll work even harder.

413
00:33:43,636 --> 00:33:45,588
Stop it!

414
00:33:46,538 --> 00:33:48,440
What? What are you looking at?

415
00:33:48,440 --> 00:33:50,209
- Nothing.
- Huh?

416
00:33:50,209 --> 00:33:54,780
You're envious again?
Better yet, find your own love.

417
00:33:54,780 --> 00:33:57,182
Or maybe you better hurry with that,

418
00:33:57,182 --> 00:33:58,717
because our wards are hungry.

419
00:33:58,717 --> 00:34:02,288
Dencio, Ms. Serafica, James and Patotina.

420
00:34:02,288 --> 00:34:04,256
- Do you know about the latest?
- What?

421
00:34:04,256 --> 00:34:05,758
The latest trending topic?

422
00:34:05,758 --> 00:34:06,892
What, what?

423
00:34:06,892 --> 00:34:09,962
Latest trending topic? I know that.

424
00:34:09,962 --> 00:34:12,598
The Lakers are the champion.

425
00:34:12,598 --> 00:34:13,732
Wrong.

426
00:34:13,732 --> 00:34:16,869
And don't count LBJ,
they won't win the championship.

427
00:34:16,869 --> 00:34:19,137
This is hotter.

428
00:34:20,339 --> 00:34:21,573
The oil prices have gone down.

429
00:34:21,573 --> 00:34:23,074
Yes, that's it.

430
00:34:24,276 --> 00:34:25,444
Wrong.

431
00:34:25,444 --> 00:34:29,148
Madam, don't hope
that the oil prices will go down.

432
00:34:29,148 --> 00:34:33,252
You're like a virgin
who believes in the love of the...

433
00:34:33,252 --> 00:34:36,655
I know it!
The wages of the workers have increased.

434
00:34:36,655 --> 00:34:39,325
- That's it.
- Right!

435
00:34:39,325 --> 00:34:40,825
Wrong!

436
00:34:42,094 --> 00:34:44,897
Someone transferred to Kapuso Network?

437
00:34:44,897 --> 00:34:47,232
- That's it.
- That's right. That's possible.

438
00:34:47,232 --> 00:34:48,701
Wrong.

439
00:34:48,701 --> 00:34:49,969
This one, I'm sure about this one.

440
00:34:49,969 --> 00:34:52,037
There's a sixth member of the Voltes 5.

441
00:34:52,037 --> 00:34:53,806
That's it.

442
00:34:53,806 --> 00:34:57,376
Wrong! What, 6? Voltes 6?

443
00:34:57,376 --> 00:34:59,044
This one.

444
00:34:59,044 --> 00:35:01,981
Finally, the crow has turned white,

445
00:35:01,981 --> 00:35:04,316
and the stork has turned black, right?

446
00:35:04,316 --> 00:35:05,718
- Yes, that's right.
- Yes, that's right.

447
00:35:05,718 --> 00:35:07,953
Just a little more push
and you'll finally get it.

448
00:35:07,953 --> 00:35:11,390
Why don't you say it?
You're full of nonsense.

449
00:35:11,390 --> 00:35:13,028
You keep on cutting corners.

450
00:35:13,028 --> 00:35:16,428
There's a news bulletin,
a hot item, what's that about?

451
00:35:16,428 --> 00:35:17,763
That's what you get.

452
00:35:17,763 --> 00:35:20,866
You're so impatient, Madam.

453
00:35:20,866 --> 00:35:22,031
What? What?

454
00:35:22,031 --> 00:35:25,037
Okay, I'm going to say it. Here it goes.

455
00:35:25,037 --> 00:35:26,405
Okay?

456
00:35:26,405 --> 00:35:27,573
- Go ahead.
- Okay?

457
00:35:27,573 --> 00:35:28,873
Okay.

458
00:35:30,009 --> 00:35:32,366
Did you know...

459
00:35:32,367 --> 00:35:35,748
that Florence Dela Cruz...

460
00:35:35,748 --> 00:35:42,955
is the missing grandchild of the Almeros?

461
00:35:42,955 --> 00:35:44,455
What?

462
00:35:52,765 --> 00:35:55,067
Are you sure Florence is an Almero?

463
00:35:55,067 --> 00:35:57,269
Dude, that's not a good joke.

464
00:35:57,269 --> 00:35:59,905
Are you saying she's the child
of the enemy of our family?

465
00:35:59,905 --> 00:36:02,907
I'm sure Nero will not joke about that.

466
00:36:03,776 --> 00:36:05,443
How did that happen?

467
00:36:06,779 --> 00:36:07,767
Based on Florence's story,

468
00:36:07,767 --> 00:36:11,434
her mother, Lydia, and father, Federico,
accidentally found her.

469
00:36:11,434 --> 00:36:15,199
So our assumption is
on the night Alyanna Almero was killed,

470
00:36:15,200 --> 00:36:17,289
she was able to hide her daughter,

471
00:36:17,289 --> 00:36:20,825
and it was Ms. Lydia and Mr. Federico
who found her.

472
00:36:22,528 --> 00:36:24,696
You know what this means, right?

473
00:36:24,696 --> 00:36:28,333
Things are about to get complicated
between Nero and Florence.

474
00:36:28,333 --> 00:36:31,302
Especially with you, because you're a Ferell.

475
00:36:46,018 --> 00:36:48,119
I'm sorry, Florence...

476
00:36:49,009 --> 00:36:52,391
But we have a reason to believe
that your parents have something to do

477
00:36:52,391 --> 00:36:55,828
with the death of your real mother,
who is Alyanna.

478
00:36:55,828 --> 00:36:56,864
Our theory is

479
00:36:56,864 --> 00:37:01,300
they're part of the group
who victimized you and your mother that day.

480
00:37:01,300 --> 00:37:04,769
But somehow, they could not do it.

481
00:37:05,971 --> 00:37:10,141
Something happened
and they decided to keep you alive.

482
00:37:13,479 --> 00:37:16,014
What you're thinking is wrong.

483
00:37:16,014 --> 00:37:17,883
My father and mother
can't possibly have done that.

484
00:37:17,883 --> 00:37:20,685
My parents are not capable of doing that.

485
00:37:22,921 --> 00:37:25,390
I grew up with them.

486
00:37:25,390 --> 00:37:29,094
So if there's someone who knows them,
that's me.

487
00:37:29,094 --> 00:37:32,964
And I can tell you
that they didn't do anything wrong.

488
00:37:33,795 --> 00:37:38,136
The little thing that we have,
they give everything to me.

489
00:37:39,138 --> 00:37:44,143
They endure sleeping on a small bed
while I sleep on a bigger one.

490
00:37:44,143 --> 00:37:47,513
The food they're about to eat,
they give it all to me.

491
00:37:47,513 --> 00:37:51,950
They opted to prioritize my studies
than think about themselves.

492
00:37:53,982 --> 00:37:56,479
Their only fault here

493
00:37:56,479 --> 00:38:00,158
is they adopted the baby
whom they thought was abandoned.

494
00:38:03,195 --> 00:38:07,032
Let's just say
that what you're saying is true,

495
00:38:07,032 --> 00:38:09,935
that they have nothing to do
with what happened to Alyanna.

496
00:38:09,935 --> 00:38:12,904
But they committed a lot of violations.

497
00:38:14,439 --> 00:38:18,210
They kept you
even if they knew you weren't their daughter,

498
00:38:18,210 --> 00:38:23,448
when the correct thing to do should've been
to report you to the authorities.

499
00:38:23,448 --> 00:38:25,484
And most likely they faked some documents

500
00:38:25,484 --> 00:38:29,220
to make it
look like you're their real daughter.

501
00:38:30,656 --> 00:38:32,691
Let's assume
that they have nothing to do with the crime.

502
00:38:32,691 --> 00:38:35,460
They were at the wrong place
at the wrong time...

503
00:38:35,460 --> 00:38:38,597
but they have a huge criminal liability.

504
00:38:38,597 --> 00:38:41,300
They have to answer that to the law.

505
00:38:41,300 --> 00:38:46,171
That's why I'm here right now.
I'm begging you.

506
00:38:46,171 --> 00:38:49,341
Is it their fault
that they wanted to become parents

507
00:38:49,341 --> 00:38:53,511
because they suddenly have a chance
to be a mother and father?

508
00:38:54,446 --> 00:38:57,549
Is it their fault
that they gave so much love to a child

509
00:38:57,549 --> 00:39:00,084
whom they thought was abandoned?

510
00:39:00,719 --> 00:39:03,006
Is it their fault

511
00:39:03,006 --> 00:39:07,125
that they created a family whom they thought
is the answer to their prayers

512
00:39:07,125 --> 00:39:09,827
because they can't have children?

513
00:39:21,473 --> 00:39:22,774
Oh, Florence.

514
00:39:22,774 --> 00:39:27,613
- Oh, Florence. Please stand up.
- I'm begging you.

515
00:39:27,613 --> 00:39:29,481
I know there's something you can do

516
00:39:29,481 --> 00:39:33,351
to help my mother and father
in this situation.

517
00:39:34,253 --> 00:39:37,389
I just want to repay the love they gave me

518
00:39:37,389 --> 00:39:41,125
ever since I was a baby
when I got separated from you.

519
00:39:42,361 --> 00:39:48,066
I will do everything to help
and protect my mother and father.

520
00:39:48,066 --> 00:39:53,871
That's why I'm begging you,
help me protect them.

521
00:40:09,388 --> 00:40:10,888
Are you okay?

522
00:40:19,031 --> 00:40:23,801
I was feeling so bad imagining
the kind of life you grew up with.

523
00:40:25,479 --> 00:40:29,326
But when you showed that kind of love
for your mother and father...

524
00:40:32,444 --> 00:40:34,245
I was reassured.

525
00:40:35,247 --> 00:40:37,716
For you to do that...

526
00:40:37,716 --> 00:40:41,285
it seems they raised you with so much love.

527
00:40:47,755 --> 00:40:50,391
I just finished talking to the lawyer.

528
00:40:51,597 --> 00:40:54,433
I'm going to make some calls
and sweep all this under the rug.

529
00:40:54,433 --> 00:40:57,768
This means they will no longer
investigate your parents.

530
00:40:58,470 --> 00:41:00,271
Thank you.

531
00:41:02,808 --> 00:41:06,110
Florence, I know how much
you love your mother and father...

532
00:41:06,820 --> 00:41:10,848
but that doesn't change the fact
that you're a real Almero.

533
00:41:11,616 --> 00:41:13,752
Look, I could never bring myself
to get married again

534
00:41:13,752 --> 00:41:16,087
after your mommy died.

535
00:41:16,855 --> 00:41:19,024
That means...

536
00:41:19,024 --> 00:41:23,427
you're the only heir
to whatever your grandfather and I have.

537
00:41:26,565 --> 00:41:29,078
What do you want me to do?

538
00:41:29,734 --> 00:41:34,573
In exchange for withdrawing the case
against your mother and father...

539
00:41:34,573 --> 00:41:37,209
you will live in this house...

540
00:41:37,209 --> 00:41:41,120
and you will forget being a Dela Cruz.

541
00:41:41,120 --> 00:41:45,783
Because from now on, you're a real Almero.

542
00:41:57,130 --> 00:41:59,998
Mr. Baste, are those my things?

543
00:41:59,998 --> 00:42:02,467
What will you do?

544
00:42:02,467 --> 00:42:04,836
I'm replacing all your old clothes
with new ones.

545
00:42:04,836 --> 00:42:06,338
Outfits that suit you better.

546
00:42:06,338 --> 00:42:09,474
And as for this...

547
00:42:09,474 --> 00:42:13,245
let's change this to a newer model
with more secure connection.

548
00:42:13,245 --> 00:42:15,933
Baste, you take care of that.

549
00:42:16,933 --> 00:42:21,953
Grandsons, you must understand
that the Almeros are a very proud family.

550
00:42:21,953 --> 00:42:24,823
They're one of the oldest families,

551
00:42:24,823 --> 00:42:28,693
and they are very sensitive
with their reputation.

552
00:42:28,693 --> 00:42:31,730
And now that Florence is with them,

553
00:42:31,730 --> 00:42:36,267
I'm sure she's going to be changed
and become an Almero.

554
00:42:59,357 --> 00:43:01,960
- Florence, can we talk?
- Can we talk later?

555
00:43:01,960 --> 00:43:04,863
I'll just find a way to talk to you.

556
00:43:04,863 --> 00:43:07,399
We're your friends, Florence.
We're not a threat.

557
00:43:07,399 --> 00:43:09,568
- Are you okay? Are they treating you well?
- Hey, don't push.

558
00:43:09,568 --> 00:43:11,470
- Don't push us.
- Hey, that's enough.

559
00:43:11,470 --> 00:43:13,839
Mister, they're not my enemies.
Don't do that.

560
00:43:13,839 --> 00:43:15,039
Don't!
